/-!
# The original Hermitian parabolic core and odd ranks

The marked natural action generates B₀/U by commutators. Since H normalizes
R = N_L(U)^∞ and U, their two-core product lies in O₂(H); thus B₀ lies
there too. The original conjugator then places all of P = O₂(I) in O₂(H).
Normality gives the reverse intersections, so V has image of order two and
I/O₂(I) identifies with the literal image of I in H/O₂(H), including its
quotient representatives. The mixed two-core of RH also displaces V only
inside B₀, and this passes to the actual two-core in N_G(U)/U. The SL₂(4) marking and residual commutation bound
also give m₃(H), m₅(H) ≤ 1 inside the original strongly quasithin normalizer.

These discharge the local action and intersection inputs in the L₃(4) row
of Aschbacher–Smith 8.2.9, printed p.720, refs/quasithin.pdf. The Chapter12
consumer supplies every input on the same selected pair. The remaining
parabolic classification and chief-section argument are not asserted here.
-/

public noncomputable section
